1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,916
Two arteries are narrowed.

2
00:00:02,299 --> 00:00:03,889
How does the team decide?

3
00:00:04,331 --> 00:00:08,406
This angiogram shows disease in more than
one coronary artery.

4
00:00:08,847 --> 00:00:14,176
The team uses the pattern of disease, the
patient’s situation and the goals of care

5
00:00:14,292 --> 00:00:15,743
to choose a plan.

6
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:21,664
Timing matters. During a heart attack, the
immediate priority is often the artery

7
00:00:21,757 --> 00:00:27,004
causing the emergency. The team then
decides whether and when to address other

8
00:00:27,062 --> 00:00:32,392
significant narrowings. With stable
coronary disease, there is usually time

9
00:00:32,426 --> 00:00:36,885
to assess symptoms, review the test
results and discuss the options.

10
00:00:37,488 --> 00:00:41,865
The team looks at where the narrowings
are, how complex they are, and how much

11
00:00:41,935 --> 00:00:43,572
heart muscle they may affect.

12
00:00:44,269 --> 00:00:46,637
It also checks how well the heart pumps.

13
00:00:47,148 --> 00:00:52,105
In selected cases, a pressure measurement
inside an artery helps determine whether a

14
00:00:52,163 --> 00:00:55,948
particular narrowing limits flow enough to
influence treatment.

15
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:01,138
Medicines and prevention are part of care
across these options.

16
00:01:01,741 --> 00:01:06,978
In stable coronary disease, treatment can
help manage symptoms and reduce the risk

17
00:01:07,036 --> 00:01:08,673
of future heart problems.

18
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:14,339
The team may discuss restoring blood flow
when symptoms still affect daily life

19
00:01:14,513 --> 00:01:17,729
or when the test results point to a
particular benefit.

20
00:01:18,542 --> 00:01:23,534
Angioplasty and stenting, also called PCI,
can open a selected

21
00:01:23,604 --> 00:01:25,612
section from inside the artery.

22
00:01:25,995 --> 00:01:29,560
A stent supports the treated section and
blood flows through it.

23
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:33,971
PCI can be suitable for particular
patterns of disease.

24
00:01:34,482 --> 00:01:39,393
The team also considers how much disease
can be treated and what risks apply.

25
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:45,059
Coronary bypass surgery uses a blood
vessel to create another route for blood

26
00:01:45,268 --> 00:01:48,170
to reach the heart muscle beyond a
narrowing.

27
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:53,929
The team may favour bypass for certain
complex patterns, including some patients

28
00:01:53,964 --> 00:01:58,550
with diabetes and disease in several
arteries, when surgery is suitable for

29
00:01:58,620 --> 00:01:59,142
them.

30
00:01:59,839 --> 00:02:04,459
When the choice is unclear, a Heart Team
can bring together a cardiologist, an

31
00:02:04,529 --> 00:02:08,128
interventional cardiologist and a cardiac
surgeon.

32
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:13,864
The team and patient discuss likely
benefits, risks, recovery, and what

33
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:15,396
matters in daily life.

34
00:02:16,093 --> 00:02:19,912
That conversation connects the test
results with a plan the patient

35
00:02:19,971 --> 00:02:21,178
understands.
